    "title": "Lorelei wins Bartenders Dolphin Tournament - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Staff Writer ,\n8 hours ago\nLONG KEY — The Lorelei Cabana Bar team claimed bragging rights at the 3rd Annual Bartenders Dolphin Tournament, held Sunday and Monday, Aug. 17-18.\nFifty-four bartenders and restaurant staff competed aboard 13 boats, with teams vying for the heaviest combined weight of three dolphinfish (mahi-mahi).\nThe Lorelei crew of Dave Ruesch, Charles Jedda, George Nance, Amberly Boeles, Erik Nessensohn and Aaron Portegys, fishing aboard Capt. Roy Lindback's Tiki, brought in fish weighing 10, 16.4, and 20.6 pounds for a winning total of 47 pounds. Their prize haul included $1,500, a perpetual trophy from King Sailfish Release Mounts and a first-place bar plaque sponsored by The Green House.\nOutstanding Captain and Mate awards went to Lindback and mates Mike Pinckney and Tommy “Spanky” Bressler.\nWahoo’s Seafood Bar and Grill placed second with 39.8 pounds, earning $500 and a trophy sponsored by C&C Wood Fired Oven. Anglers Amber Spaulding, Dominica Bevevino and Chrissy Cox fished aboard Capt. Cole Tristram’s charter boat Renegade.\nHungry Tarpon Restaurant took third with 29.7 pounds, winning $250 and a trophy sponsored by the Islander. The team consisted of James Davis, Donald Reilford, Nick Berrios and David Prouty fishing aboard the Contagious with Capt. Brian Cone\nTop angler awards went to Lorelei’s George Nance (20.6 pounds), Wahoo’s Dominica Bevevino (16.9 pounds) and Lorelei’s Dave Ruesch (16.4 pounds).",
